  "version": "1.0.0",
  "status": "testing",
  "notes": "One adapter covers One-Time Registration and the CGL/CHSL/GD application forms because SSC reuses the OTR profile across every examination — the application form re-displays the registered particulars rather than asking for them again, so the same label set applies. Matching is label-driven: SSC's Angular front end generates its control names (formcontrolname=\"ctrl_12\"), so a hand-written selector would be a guess that rots at the next release. Class 10 is SSC's 'Matriculation', which is why the matriculation fields below map onto the registry's customer.education.class10.* block. SSC treats the matriculation-certificate spelling of the name as authoritative and shows it beside the Hindi rendering, so candidate_name_hi claims both labels.",
  "knownIssues": "Identification Marks (SSC asks for two visible marks) has no equivalent in the customer field registry, so it is left to the operator — proposing one from any existing field would be a confident wrong answer. Adding customer.identification_marks is a product decision under docs/SECURITY.md §4, not an adapter change. Full Aadhaar is deliberately absent: only customer.aadhaar_last4 is mapped, matching the last-4 control SSC's OTR actually shows. SSC's captcha and the OTP step are never touched (spec §2 prohibits both). Category, date of birth and the Aadhaar last-4 are high_risk fields, so each is marked reviewRequired regardless of adapter confidence.",
  "documentRequirements": [
    {
      "key": "photo",
      "label": "Applicant photograph (20–50 KB JPEG, name and date stamped)",
      "presetCode": "ssc.photo",
      "required": true,
      "notes": "Captured live through the portal's webcam step at OTR, or uploaded as a 20–50 KB JPEG. SSC rejects a photograph that does not carry the applicant's name and the date of capture printed on it, and one taken more than three months earlier."
    },
    {
      "key": "signature",
      "label": "Signature (10–20 KB JPEG)",
      "presetCode": "ssc.signature",
      "required": true,
      "notes": "Black or blue ink on plain white paper, 10–20 KB JPEG. SSC rejects a signature written in capital letters."
    }
  ],
